A certain 2-page comic from Mauri Kunnas' Nyrok City
collection ("The Giant Gollexön - The Best and the Wörst of
Nyrok City") has caught my eye.

Paul Oxley is the hero of this story, which borrows some of it's
elements from Enid Blyton's books. Paul has escaped from
the UK due political reasons. He's alone, accompanied only
by Tim the dog (Timo in Finnish) and the "cave is looong".

Paul has to eat Tim in order to survive.

Mr. Kunnas has kindly included a translation of the text in this
particular "issue", which I hereby quote.
Paul says to himself: "Oh boy. Poison in my dog."

After that, he finds a hatch which leads to a stage in a certain
music club in Finland... and there's a band playing "new wave s**t".
Now the aggravate monster -intrinsic kicks in. Thousands of fresh
admirers of Paul start chasing him. Paul heads back to the cave.
However, the story has a happy ending which I will not spoil here.

